params.description:
Symbol to get data for.;
    Symbol to get data for.Default is 'VX_EOD'. Entered dates return the data nearest to the entered date.
    'VX_AM' = Mid-Morning TWAP Levels
    'VX_EOD' = 4PM Eastern Time Levels (provider: cboe);
    Symbol to get data for. The underlying root, as it appears in the instrument name. (provider: deribit)

Filter series by text in the indicator name. Supports '+' (AND), '|' (OR), and "quoted phrases". (provider: ecb);
    The search query string. Multiple search phrases can be separated by semicolons. Each phrase can use AND (+) and OR (|) operators, as well as quoted phrases. Semicolon separation allows commas to be used within search phrases. Multiple comma separated items allowed. (provider: imf);
    Search string. Use quotes for exact phrases, + for AND, | for OR. e.g. 'GDP growth', 'CPI | inflation', 'balance +trade'. (provider: oecd)

The frequency of the data.  Monthly is valid only for ['main', 'summary']. (provider: ecb);
    Reporting frequency. (provider: imf);
    Frequency of the data. (provider: oecd)

The country/region of the data.  This parameter will override the 'report_type' parameter. (provider: ecb);
    The country to get data. Enter as a 3-letter ISO country code, default is USA. (provider: fred);
    The country to get data. Multiple comma separated items allowed. (provider: imf);
    The country to get data. Multiple comma separated items allowed. (provider: oecd)

The country to get data. Multiple comma separated items allowed for provider(s): imf, oecd.;
    ISO3 country code(s). Use comma-separated values for multiple countries. Validated against the dataflow's available countries via constraint API. (provider: imf);
    Country name or ISO code. Comma-separated for multiples. 'all' for all. (provider: oecd)

The frequency of the data.;
    The frequency of the data. Choices vary by indicator and country. Common options: 'annual', 'quarter', 'month'. Use 'all' or '*' to return all available frequencies. Direct IMF codes (e.g., 'A', 'Q', 'M') are also accepted. (provider: imf);
    Frequency: 'annual'/'yearly', 'quarterly'/'quarter', 'monthly'/'month', or SDMX code (A/Q/M). (provider: oecd)

The fact to lookup, typically a GAAP-reporting measure. Choices vary by provider.;
    Fact or concept from the SEC taxonomy, in UpperCamelCase. Defaults to, 'Revenues'. AAPL, MSFT, GOOG, BRK-A currently report revenue as, 'RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax'. In previous years, they have reported as 'Revenues'.
Facts fall into two groups. Instantaneous balance-sheet concepts are measured at a point in time (e.g. 'Assets', 'Liabilities', 'StockholdersEquity', 'Goodwill', 'LongTermDebt'); the full set is openbb_sec.utils.definitions.INSTANT_FACTS. Everything else is a flow concept from the income or cash-flow statement, measured over a period (e.g. 'Revenues', 'NetIncomeLoss', 'NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities'). The 'instantaneous' parameter and the standalone-Q4 derivation apply only to flow concepts; balance-sheet concepts are always point-in-time, including the year-end (Q4) value. (provider: sec)

The reporting period. Nasdaq publishes the last four periods of each statement. (provider: nasdaq);
    Time period of the data to return. For balance sheet, TTM is treated as the average of the last 4 quarters. (provider: sec);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: tmx);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: yfinance)

The reporting period. Nasdaq publishes the last four periods of each statement. (provider: nasdaq);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: sec);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: tmx);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: yfinance)

The reporting period. Nasdaq publishes the last four periods of each statement. (provider: nasdaq);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: sec);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: tmx);
    Time period of the data to return. (provider: yfinance)

Time interval of the data to return. The most recent trading day is not including in daily historical data. Intraday data is only available for the most recent trading day at 1 minute intervals. (provider: cboe);
    Time interval of the data to return. Or, any integer (entered as a string) representing the number of minutes. Default is daily data. There is no extended hours data, and intraday data is limited to after April 12 2022. (provider: tmx);
    Time interval of the data to return. (provider: yfinance)

Filter by country. Accepts country names, ISO 3166-1 alpha-2/alpha-3 codes, or 'all' for all countries. Multiple comma-separated values allowed. Multiple comma separated items allowed. (provider: nasdaq);
    Two-letter country code, or None for every market. (provider: tmx);
    Filter by country. Accepts ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes (e.g., 'US', 'DE'), alpha-3 codes (e.g., 'USA'), country names (e.g., 'United States'), or 'all' for all countries. (provider: yfinance)

Limit the number of results to return. (provider: nasdaq);
    The maximum number of results to return. (provider: tmx);
    Limit the number of results returned. Default is, 200. Set to, 0, for all results. (provider: yfinance)

When True, the company directory will be cached for 24 hours. Set as False to bypass. (provider: cboe);
    Whether to use the cache or not. (provider: sec);
    Whether to use the on-disk response cache. Set to False to bypass. (provider: tmx)

Time interval of the data to return. The most recent trading day is not including in daily historical data. Intraday data is only available for the most recent trading day at 1 minute intervals. (provider: cboe);
    Time interval of the data to return. Or, any integer (entered as a string) representing the number of minutes. Default is daily data. There is no extended hours data, and intraday data is limited to after April 12 2022. (provider: tmx);
    Time interval of the data to return. (provider: yfinance)

Time interval of the data to return. The most recent trading day is not including in daily historical data. Intraday data is only available for the most recent trading day at 1 minute intervals. (provider: cboe);
    The data interval. One-minute data covers the current session only and ignores the date range. (provider: nasdaq);
    Time interval of the data to return. (provider: yfinance)

The region of focus for the data - i.e., us, eu.;
    The region of focus for the data - i.e., us, eu, au. 'au' covers the Cboe Australia (CXA) indices. (provider: cboe);
    The index universe to return. Nordic indexes are served from the Nasdaq Nordic listing. (provider: nasdaq);
    The region the indices are published for. (provider: tmx)
